==Battleground==
*2 [[Haniwanwan]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*4 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Corporal Weyland]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns.
**1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns.
**1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns.
**1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns.
**2 [[Corporal Weyland]]s spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[Axoloty|Axoloties]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Use high damaging cats such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] at the start to get rid of the Haniwanwans alongside the Relic Doges. If the Relic Doges push too much, summon some [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]. The Relic Doges and Haniwanwans are your main cash source here, so try to defeat them with Can Can Cat (with Bounty talent unlocked). Once you've hit the base, spam meatshields such as [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], and [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]]. Note, do not use any knockback resistant/immune cats, as they would be a stepping stone for the Axoloties to hit. Constantly spam your meatshields along with Slapstick Cats to fight the M. Ost. When the 2nd Axoloty spawns and presumably fails to hit you, stop spawning for a while and lure the M. Ost closer to your base. This is to prevent accidental knockbacks of the 3 Axolotyls which would trigger their attack animations again. If you think an Axoloty is going to hit you, spawn an [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], just to be safe. After defeating the M. Ost, use any means you like to defeat the 3 Axoloties and destroy the base.

